From: SAGA <saga@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: BORE discount for cgroup-marked latency-sensitive tasks (top-app)

Incremental on top of the "bore" addon (bore-android14-6.1-v6.8.0.patch).
Requires that addon to have already run in the same ADDONS= list -- this
patch's context is the post-BORE-patch state of kernel/sched/fair.c and
kernel/sysctl.c, not stock ACK.

Problem: BORE's effective_prio() only looks at behavioral history
(se->burst_penalty, built from accumulated runtime since last
sleep/yield). It has no notion of *why* a task matters -- it cannot
distinguish a freshly-launched foreground app (which hasn't built up
a "well-behaved" burst history yet) from a background task that
happens to also sleep/wake a lot. Cold-starts and app-switches are
exactly the case where this blind spot shows up as jank.

Android already carries the signal BORE is missing: cpu.uclamp.latency_sensitive
on a task's cgroup (task_group(p)->latency_sensitive, CONFIG_UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP,
already =y in gki_defconfig -- see kernel/sched/sched.h and the
uclamp.latency_sensitive cgroup file in kernel/sched/core.c). Userspace
(ActivityManager / cpuset) already sets this bit to 1 for the top-app
cgroup. This patch just wires BORE's priority calculation to read it.

Change: effective_prio() now subtracts a bounded, sysctl-tunable
discount (sched_bore_topapp_discount, default 6, range 0-39, same
range as the priority delta itself) from the burst-penalty-derived
priority addition when task_group(p)->latency_sensitive is set. It is
a strict discount, never a boost past the task's non-BORE baseline
priority (min_t floor at the existing burst_penalty=0 case), so a
misconfigured cgroup cannot starve everything else -- it can only make
BORE cheaper for tasks Android already flagged as foreground-critical.

Default of 6 chosen to be noticeable but modest (max possible
effective_prio addition is 39); tune via
/proc/sys/kernel/sched_bore_topapp_discount at runtime, same as the
existing sched_burst_* knobs, no rebuild needed to A/B it.

Signed-off-by: SAGA <saga@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c   | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 kernel/sysctl.c       | 12 +++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 540f2bdd7..a1b2c3d4e 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -136,6 +136,7 @@ u8   __read_mostly sched_bore                  = 1;
 u8   __read_mostly sched_burst_inherit_type    = 2;
 u8   __read_mostly sched_burst_smoothness      = 1;
 u8   __read_mostly sched_burst_penalty_offset  = 24;
+u8   __read_mostly sched_bore_topapp_discount  = 6;
 unsigned int __read_mostly sched_burst_penalty_scale   = 1536;
 unsigned int __read_mostly sched_burst_cache_lifetime  = 75000000;
 #endif
@@ -607,13 +608,33 @@ static inline u32 calc_burst_penalty(u64 burst_time)
 	return scaled_penalty - (overflow & ~(overflow >> 31));
 }
 
+/*
+ * True when the task's cgroup has been marked latency-sensitive by
+ * userspace (Android sets this for the top-app cgroup via the
+ * cpu.uclamp.latency_sensitive cgroup file). Returns false, not an
+ * error, whenever the field isn't compiled in or the task has no
+ * group -- callers treat "unknown" the same as "not top-app".
+ */
+#ifdef CONFIG_UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP
+static inline bool bore_topapp_boosted(struct task_struct *p)
+{
+	struct task_group *tg = task_group(p);
+
+	return tg && tg->latency_sensitive;
+}
+#else
+static inline bool bore_topapp_boosted(struct task_struct *p)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+#endif
+
 static inline u8 effective_prio(struct task_struct *p)
 {
 	u8 prio = p->static_prio - MAX_RT_PRIO;
 
-	if (likely(sched_bore))
-		prio += p->se.burst_penalty >> 8;
+	if (likely(sched_bore)) {
+		u8 penalty = p->se.burst_penalty >> 8;
+
+		if (sched_bore_topapp_discount && bore_topapp_boosted(p))
+			penalty -= min_t(u8, penalty, sched_bore_topapp_discount);
+
+		prio += penalty;
+	}
 
 	return min_t(u8, 39, prio);
 }
diff --git a/kernel/sysctl.c b/kernel/sysctl.c
index 3d71a97d6..f9e8a7b21 100644
--- a/kernel/sysctl.c
+++ b/kernel/sysctl.c
@@ -108,6 +108,7 @@ extern u8 sched_burst_inherit_type;
 extern u8 sched_burst_smoothness;
 extern u8 sched_burst_penalty_offset;
 extern uint sched_burst_penalty_scale;
+extern u8 sched_bore_topapp_discount;
 extern uint sched_burst_cache_lifetime;
 extern int sched_bore_update_handler(struct ctl_table *table, int write,
 	void __user *buffer, size_t *lenp, loff_t *ppos);
+static int __maybe_unused thirty_nine = 39;
@@ -1722,6 +1723,15 @@ static struct ctl_table kern_table[] = {
 		.mode		= 0644,
 		.proc_handler	= proc_douintvec,
 	},
+	{
+		.procname	= "sched_bore_topapp_discount",
+		.data		= &sched_bore_topapp_discount,
+		.maxlen		= sizeof(u8),
+		.mode		= 0644,
+		.proc_handler	= proc_dou8vec_minmax,
+		.extra1		= SYSCTL_ZERO,
+		.extra2		= &thirty_nine,
+	},
 #endif
 	{
 		.procname	= "sysctl_writes_strict",
